# Documentation standards

Canonical rule: `rules/dev/documentation-standards.md`. The data — human-facing globs, footer URLs, the init line — lives in `config/docs/`; never restate it.

- **Every diagram is a fenced ```mermaid block**, never box-drawing or ASCII art (a directory tree in a ```text fence is not a diagram). Its first line is the canonical init directive from `config/docs/mermaid-init.txt`, copied verbatim; no `classDef` / `class` / `style` / `fill:` inside a block. Dark is the default; one block may keep another palette when the line above its fence reads `<!-- doc-standards-ok: <reason> -->`.
- **Every human-facing doc** (`README.md`, `docs/**` minus `docs/agent-guidelines/**`, `docs/changelog/**`, `docs/CHANGELOG.md`) **ends with the same centred footer**: a `---` rule, then one `<p align="center">` with `Have a Question?` and `Open an Issue` separated by `&nbsp;·&nbsp;`. `README.md` keeps its `MIT © …` line directly above it.
- Never type the footer: `bash scripts/check-doc-standards.sh --fix` appends or repairs it from the config. `make check-doc-standards` (in `make validate`) fails on any violation; `--strict` also flags box-drawing lines.
